--- log ---
2026-05-08T08:00Z MinhHaDuong created

2026-05-08T14:24Z MinhHaDuong closed — autoclosed — PR #107
--- body ---
## Context

`erg migrate` calls `cmdInit` at the end of its layout upgrade step, and
`cmdInit` refuses if `tickets/erg` is absent ("requires tickets/erg to already
exist"). This means a project that has never had the binary placed yet cannot
bootstrap itself with `erg migrate` alone — the user must manually copy the
binary first, then run migrate.

The intended workflow is: from any project root, run
`~/.local/bin/erg migrate` and have it fully bootstrap that project (binary +
specs + AGENTS.md + layout cleanup). Making the user remember a pre-step
defeats this.

The fix is straightforward: the running binary already knows its own path
(`os.Executable()`). If `tickets/erg` is absent at the point where `cmdInit`
would be called, copy the running binary there first, then call `cmdInit`
normally.

## Actions

1. In the `migrate` command handler, before calling `cmdInit`, check whether
   `tickets/erg` exists.
2. If absent, copy the running binary (`os.Executable()`) to `tickets/erg`
   and set it executable (`chmod 0755`).
3. Then call `cmdInit` as usual — it will find the binary and proceed.
4. Print a one-line message: `copied binary → tickets/erg`.

## Test

```
# Create a scratch project with a ticket store but no binary
mkdir -p /tmp/test-migrate/tickets
touch /tmp/test-migrate/tickets/0001-placeholder.erg
cd /tmp/test-migrate

# Run migrate — should self-copy binary and unpack init assets
~/.local/bin/erg migrate

# Verify
test -x tickets/erg          || echo FAIL: binary missing
test -f tickets/AGENTS.md    || echo FAIL: AGENTS.md missing
test -f tickets/spec-erg-v1.md || echo FAIL: spec missing
echo PASS
```

## Exit criteria

- `erg migrate` run from a project without `tickets/erg` succeeds and
  leaves a working binary at `tickets/erg`.
- `erg migrate` run when `tickets/erg` already exists is idempotent
  (does not overwrite).
- `erg init` (called separately) continues to refuse if binary is absent
  — its pre-condition is unchanged; only `migrate` gets the self-copy logic.
